# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# Negative tests at the UI PD's boundaries. Each probe holds the
# memory grants of the display PD or the UI PD in ui-demo.system and makes
# one access they do not allow; each must fault, be caught by the parent and
# reported, and the display side must answer after each one with its private
# page intact.
#
# The order follows from the priorities in ui-isolation.system (one core).
# Fault lines name what was accessed and why it failed, not code addresses
# or translation levels, so they do not change from build to build; the
# "fault detail" lines that follow them carry those and are not checked.
NOWAYOS: isolation-parent: starting; children display_writes_framebuffer (0), ui_writes_display_index (1), ui_reads_display_private (2) and ui_reads_device (3)
NOWAYOS: isolation-bystander: starting; private page at 0x60000000 holds 0x5afec0de
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: display_writes_framebuffer read 0x00000000 from its read-only framebuffer at 0x50000000
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: display_writes_framebuffer writing to its read-only framebuffer at 0x50000000
NOWAYOS: isolation-parent: display_writes_framebuffer stopped: data write at 0x50000000: permission fault (the mapping does not allow it)
NOWAYOS: isolation-bystander: still running (check 1); private page intact
NOWAYOS: isolation-parent: bystander answered after fault 1
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: ui_writes_display_index read 0x00000000 from its read-only view of the display's index on the Present ring at 0x40001000
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: ui_writes_display_index writing to its read-only view of the display's index on the Present ring at 0x40001000
NOWAYOS: isolation-parent: ui_writes_display_index stopped: data write at 0x40001000: permission fault (the mapping does not allow it)
NOWAYOS: isolation-bystander: still running (check 2); private page intact
NOWAYOS: isolation-parent: bystander answered after fault 2
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: ui_reads_display_private wrote 0x00ffffff to its framebuffer at 0x50000000 and read it back
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: ui_reads_display_private reading 0x60000000 (where display_side keeps its private page), which is not mapped in this PD
NOWAYOS: isolation-parent: ui_reads_display_private stopped: data read at 0x60000000: translation fault (nothing mapped there)
NOWAYOS: isolation-bystander: still running (check 3); private page intact
NOWAYOS: isolation-parent: bystander answered after fault 3
NOWAYOS: isolation-probe: ui_reads_device reading 0x9000000 (the physical address of QEMU's PL011 UART), which is not mapped in this PD
NOWAYOS: isolation-parent: ui_reads_device stopped: data read at 0x9000000: translation fault (nothing mapped there)
NOWAYOS: isolation-bystander: still running (check 4); private page intact
NOWAYOS: isolation-parent: bystander answered after fault 4
NOWAYOS: ui-isolation: 4 of 4 forbidden accesses faulted and were contained; bystander still running

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# a forbidden access that succeeded, a fault the monitor had to handle (a PD
# other than a probe faulted), a kernel error message (such as a fault reply
# left pending), a panic, or anything unexpected.
!ISOLATION FAILURE
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!CHANGED
!cannot
!unexpected
!NOT stopped
!no probe is defined
!no test is defined
